{'bigquery-public-data': {'noaa_gsod': [], 'noaa_historic_severe_storms': [], 'noaa_hurricanes': ['hurricanes'], 'noaa_icoads': [], 'noaa_passive_acoustic_index': [], 'noaa_passive_bioacoustic': [], 'noaa_pifsc_metadata': [], 'noaa_preliminary_severe_storms': [], 'noaa_significant_earthquakes': [], 'noaa_tsunami': []}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they are used (all come from  
`bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`):

`season`: filter rows to the year 2020.  
`basin`: keep only North‑Atlantic rows (`'NA'`).  
`sid`: unique storm identifier – used to group all points that belong to the same hurricane.  
`iso_time`: timestamp – provides the chronological order of the track.  
`latitude` / `longitude`: coordinates required to build geography points and measure travel distance.  
`usa_wind`: 1‑minute maximum sustained wind speed reported by the U.S. agency (the standard for the N. Atlantic).  
(Any row whose `usa_wind` is NULL can still stay in the path; the value will simply remain NULL.)

Principal filter‑conditions that will be used  
`WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'`

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Ten exploratory → increasingly complex SQL queries
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

```sql
--Description: 1) See which seasons exist in the table.
SELECT DISTINCT `season`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Look at a small sample of North‑Atlantic 2020 rows.
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) List every 2020 N. Atlantic storm identifier and its name.
SELECT DISTINCT sid, name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'
ORDER BY sid
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) How many track‑points does each 2020 N. Atlantic storm have?
SELECT sid, COUNT(*) AS pts
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_hurricanes.hurricanes`
WHERE basin = 'NA' AND season = '2020'
GROUP BY sid
ORDER BY pts DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

